cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the article that describes the
  formats and the architectures (preferred citation below).
title: "high-radix-fp-fpga: VHDL floating-point adders, multipliers and converters for high-radix formats on FPGAs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hormigo
    given-names: Javier
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5454-6821"
    affiliation: "Departamento de Arquitectura de Computadores, Universidad de Málaga"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/fjhormigouma/high-radix-fp-fpga"
abstract: >-
  Synthesizable VHDL floating-point adders, multipliers and IEEE-754
  converters for high-radix formats (radix 16, 64, 256, 4096 and 2^24) aimed
  at FPGA implementation, together with a Python reference model and
  self-checking GHDL tests.
keywords:
  - floating-point arithmetic
  - high-radix formats
  - floating-point adder
  - floating-point multiplier
  - FPGA
  - VHDL
  - computer arithmetic
